From d2f932c27242e550e587db4b09b515412d24e203 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emdee52 <emdee7101@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:26:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] port(PF-10-paint-marks): merged support passes keep their
 transition, weave and contact marks

merge_duplicate_support_layers composed fills and islands only, so every pass but the first at a print_z lost the SU-8/9/10 marks recorded on its layer - with support painting that is the automatic/default pass (which runs last) and every tree region. Carry the marks onto the merged layer, and drop the base layer's zone family tags when appending so untagged fills are not emitted nowhere. The paint row's support_type field was dead data (the dispatcher forces the manual engine on purpose); drop it and say so.
---
 src/libslic3r/OrcaExt/SupportPaintTypes.cpp |  5 --
 src/libslic3r/OrcaExt/SupportPaintTypes.hpp |  7 +-
 src/libslic3r/PrintObject.cpp               | 16 ++++-
 src/libslic3r/Support/SupportCommon.cpp     | 26 ++++++++
 src/libslic3r/Support/SupportCommon.hpp     |  4 ++
 tests/fff_print/test_support_material.cpp   | 72 +++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 122 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

